    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to bolster our secondary categories. **Corbin Carroll** (78.18) and **Jose Caballero** (78.35) headline our offensive output; **Caballero** is a particularly high-leverage start today as he faces a left-handed pitcher, providing a significant +13% platoon edge that juices his scoring potential. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **James Wood** (70.07) are locked into strong starting positions, with **Wood** providing an elite 0.407 xwOBA profile that makes him a foundational piece of our lineup despite facing a neutral right-handed platoon. These players, combined with **Austin Riley** (65.47) and **Gabriel Moreno** (65.57), are positioned to thrive against shaky starters like Aldegheri and Whisenhunt, both of whom carry xERAs north of 5.40.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Dalton Rushing**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 39.25 score. While **Rushing** benefit from a pitcher with a slower delivery, which generally facilitates our high-priority stolen base targets, he fell just short of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor due to a disadvantageous left-on-left matchup against McClanahan. Consequently, **Alex Freeland** (41.24) remains in the lineup despite the tough matchup, as his switch-hitting versatility offers slightly more structural value than **Rushing** on this specific roster construction. We remain cautious of **Brice Turang** (53.12), whose score is suppressed by his elite matchup against a pitcher with a high hold rate for stolen bases; he remains a start, but his floor is lower than typical given the opposing defensive battery's skill in neutralizing our primary weapon.",
